# Public testnet soak fleet. One node per line:
#   role   ssh-target              rpc              logfile
#
# role is one of: base (current release, never faulted), cand (release candidate),
# val (candidate + bond, actually attesting), churn (candidate, faulted on schedule),
# strag (older binary AND older consensus params — its handshake must be REFUSED).
#
# The baselines are the control. Faulting them destroys the only reference for
# "is this the network or is this the candidate", so the fault scripts must
# never target a base row.
#
# base   root@203.0.113.10      127.0.0.1:16110  /var/log/kaspad-tn.log
# base   root@203.0.113.11      127.0.0.1:16110  /var/log/kaspad-tn.log
# cand   root@203.0.113.20      127.0.0.1:16110  /var/log/kaspad-tn.log
# val    root@203.0.113.30      127.0.0.1:16110  /var/log/kaspad-tn.log
# churn  root@203.0.113.40      127.0.0.1:16110  /var/log/kaspad-tn.log
# strag  root@203.0.113.50      127.0.0.1:16110  /var/log/kaspad-tn.log
